==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ru|orv|сꙋка}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*sǫka}} (compare {{cog|pl|suka}}), ultimately from a derivative of {{der|ru|ine-pro|*ḱwṓ}}. Cognates include {{cog|hy|շուն||dog}}, {{cog|de|Hund||dog}}, {{cog|grc|κύων||dog}}, {{cog|ga|cú||dog}}, {{cog|la|canis||dog}}, {{cog|fa|سگ||dog‎}}, {{cog|sa|श्वन्||dog}}, {{cog|en|hound}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|су́ка}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-сука.ogg|Audio}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|су́ка|a=an}}

# [[bitch]] {{gloss|female dog}}
# {{lb|ru|vulgar|offensive}} [[bitch]]; [[contemptible]] person, usually but not necessarily female
